# Design system workflow

Use `$ARGUMENTS` to define the product or UI surface. Inspect the existing visual language, components, accessibility rules, assets, and theme configuration before proposing changes.

Document reusable decisions for color, typography, spacing, layout, motion, states, responsive behavior, and accessibility. Reuse existing primitives and tokens before adding new ones. Keep the system framework-agnostic unless the repository establishes a specific UI stack.

Deliver a short rationale, affected components, migration risks, visual acceptance criteria, and a verification plan. Do not change application code unless implementation is explicitly requested.
